1
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:09,260
الحمدلله رب العالمين و الصلاة و السلام على سيد الأنبياء و المرسلين و على آله و صحبه و من استن بسنته إلى يوم الدين

2
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:15,978
اللهم اجعلنا منهم و من الذين آمنو و عملوا الصالحات و تواصو بالحق و تواصو بالصبر أمين يا رب العلمين ثم أما بعد

3
00:00:16,291 --> 00:00:18,458
السلام عليكم و رحمة الله تعالى وبركاته

4
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:27,578
The first thing I'm going to do, this is our first case study of symmetrical structures or ring passages inside passages of the Qurʾān.

5
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,160
So it's just, it's still at the level of passages.

6
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:33,980
The first example I'd like to give you of that is Ibrahim ﷺ and the Ka'bah

7
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,860
as described in Surat al Baqarah.

8
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:39,860
And this is Āyahs number 121 or 122

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:46,460
all the way to 133. So 122 to 133.

10
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:47,800
Okay?

11
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:49,950
And the first thing I'm going to do is I'm going to recite

12
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:52,680
or read the translation of all of these Āyāt to you.

13
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,510
So you have an idea of the subject matter,

14
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,810
and then we're going to try to make some associations.

15
00:00:56,820 --> 00:01:01,979
يَـٰبَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱذْكُرُوا۟ نِعْمَتِىَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَنِّى فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

16
00:01:02,011 --> 00:01:09,289
Children of Israel, Sons of Israel, make mention of the favour I showered upon you and I gave you preference over all other nations.

17
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:12,150
وَٱتَّقُوا۟ يَوْمًۭالَّا تَجْزِى نَفْسٌ عَن نَّفْسٍۢ شَيْـًۭٔا

18
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:18,596
and be mindful and fearful of a day on which no person will be able to compensate on behalf of another in any way,

19
00:01:18,716 --> 00:01:20,366
وَلَا يُقْبَلُ مِنْهَا عَدْلٌۭ

20
00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:22,736
nor will an equivalent ever be taken at all,

21
00:01:22,846 --> 00:01:24,346
وَلَا تَنفَعُهَا شَفَـٰعَةٌۭ

22
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:26,906
and nor shall intercession be of any benefit

23
00:01:26,916 --> 00:01:28,096
وَلَا هُمْ يُنصَرُونَ

24
00:01:28,086 --> 00:01:29,356
nor will they be aided.

25
00:01:31,266 --> 00:01:33,992
وَإِذِ ٱبْتَلَىٰٓ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ رَبُّهُۥ بِكَلِمَـٰتٍۢ فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ ۖ

26
00:01:34,017 --> 00:01:40,312
And when we thoroughly tested Ibrahim, or when His Master thoroughly tested Ibrahim,

27
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:42,372
with certain instructions

28
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:43,690
فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ

29
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,800
and he fulfilled every last one of them.

30
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:47,950
قَالَ إِنِّى جَاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ إِمَامًۭا ۖ

31
00:01:48,153 --> 00:01:53,013
He said 'No doubt, I am making you--I have made you a leader over all people.'

32
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:54,622
قَالَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِى ۖ

33
00:01:54,612 --> 00:01:58,364
He said: 'What of my children?', What of my offspring, my future lineage?

34
00:01:58,434 --> 00:02:00,604
قَالَ لَا يَنَالُ عَهْدِى ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ

35
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:03,924
He said: 'My guarantee does not extend wrongdoers'.

36
00:02:04,184 --> 00:02:07,164
وَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا ٱلْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةًۭ لِّلنَّاسِ وَأَمْنًۭا

37
00:02:07,374 --> 00:02:11,951
And when We made the house a place to come back to for people, and a place to find peace

38
00:02:12,081 --> 00:02:14,459
وَٱتَّخِذُوا۟ مِن مَّقَامِ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ مُصَلًّۭى ۖ

39
00:02:14,709 --> 00:02:19,519
And take, all of you, a place to pray by the station of Ibrahim, مَّقَامِ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ.

40
00:02:20,229 --> 00:02:23,349
ۖ وَعَهِدْنَآ إِلَىٰٓ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ وَإِسْمَـٰعِيلَ أَن طَهِّرَا بَيْتِىَ

41
00:02:23,509 --> 00:02:30,099
And We had taken a promise, a covenant from Ibrahim and Isma'il, that they should both purify My House

42
00:02:30,089 --> 00:02:32,961
بَيْتِىَ لِلطَّآئِفِينَ وَٱلْعَـٰكِفِينَ وَٱلرُّكَّعِ ٱلسُّجُودِ

43
00:02:33,171 --> 00:02:35,921
For those who do Ṭawāf, those who go around the Ka'bah,

44
00:02:36,111 --> 00:02:40,640
those who do Iʿtikāf, those who stay there, devoting their time into that sanctuary.

45
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:44,445
And those who bow and those who go into prostration, rukūʿand sujūd.

46
00:02:45,115 --> 00:02:48,045
وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمُ رَبِّ ٱجْعَلْ هَـٰذَا بَلَدًا ءَامِنًۭا

47
00:02:48,105 --> 00:02:53,645
When Abraham said, Ibrahim (عليه السلام) said, make this into a peaceful city, a safe city.

48
00:02:54,115 --> 00:02:55,735
وَٱرْزُقْ أَهْلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ

49
00:02:55,735 --> 00:02:57,815
and provide its citizens all kinds of fruit

50
00:02:57,845 --> 00:03:00,247
مَنْ ءَامَنَ مِنْهُم بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلْيَوْمِ ٱلْـَٔاخِرِ ۖ

51
00:03:00,337 --> 00:03:02,837
Whoever of them were to believe in Allah and the last day

52
00:03:02,907 --> 00:03:04,066
قَالَ وَمَن كَفَرَ

53
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:06,083
Allah responded, and whoever were to disbelieve

54
00:03:06,083 --> 00:03:07,669
فَأُمَتِّعُهُۥ قَلِيلًۭا

55
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:11,659
Then I will let him enjoy, or I will give him to enjoy a little bit as well.

56
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:13,899
ثُمَّ أَضْطَرُّهُۥٓ إِلَىٰ عَذَابِ ٱلنَّارِ ۖ

57
00:03:14,129 --> 00:03:17,719
Thereafter, I am going to drag him into the punishment of the fire

58
00:03:17,859 --> 00:03:18,630
وَبِئْسَ ٱلْمَصِير

59
00:03:18,629 --> 00:03:20,349
And what a terrible place to be, that is.

60
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:23,950
وَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمُ ٱلْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ ٱلْبَيْتِ وَإِسْمَـٰعِيلُ

61
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:32,750
And as Abraham, Ibrahim عليه السلام was raising the foundations of the House, from the bottom of the House, along with Isma'il,

62
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,930
رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّآ ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ

63
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:39,990
Master, accept from us both of us, certainly You are the All-Hearing, All-Knowing.

64
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:42,210
رَبَّنَا وَٱجْعَلْنَا مُسْلِمَيْنِ لَكَ

65
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,630
Master, make both of us Muslim before You, submissive before You.

66
00:03:45,805 --> 00:03:48,305
لَكَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِنَآ أُمَّةًۭ مُّسْلِمَةًۭ لَّكَ

67
00:03:48,385 --> 00:03:54,915
and out of our offspring, a nation at least, a group, that will remain submissive to You, remain Muslim to You.

68
00:03:55,205 --> 00:03:57,345
لَّكَ وَأَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَا وَتُبْ عَلَيْنَآ ۖ

69
00:03:57,475 --> 00:04:00,375
and show us our rituals and accept our repentance.

70
00:04:00,335 --> 00:04:02,295
إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ

71
00:04:02,385 --> 00:04:07,247
Certainly, You are the one who continually and repeatedly accepts repentance and is always loving and caring.

72
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:09,451
رَبَّنَا وَٱبْعَثْ فِيهِمْ رَسُولًۭا مِّنْهُمْ

73
00:04:09,581 --> 00:04:14,301
Master appoint from among them, a Messenger who comes  from within them.

74
00:04:14,521 --> 00:04:16,281
يَتْلُوا۟ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَايَـٰتِكَ

75
00:04:16,291 --> 00:04:19,651
he will recite your miraculous signs onto them,

76
00:04:19,861 --> 00:04:21,641
وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ وَٱلْحِكْمَةَ

77
00:04:21,731 --> 00:04:23,784
and he will teach them the book and the wisdom,

78
00:04:23,774 --> 00:04:24,804
وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ ۚ

79
00:04:24,814 --> 00:04:25,804
and he will cleanse them,

80
00:04:25,914 --> 00:04:27,654
إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ

81
00:04:27,914 --> 00:04:30,864
Certainly, You are the Ultimate Authority, Ultimately Wise.

82
00:04:31,114 --> 00:04:34,464
وَمَن يَرْغَبُ عَن مِّلَّةِ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ إِلَّا مَن سَفِهَ نَفْسَهُۥ ۚ

83
00:04:34,674 --> 00:04:39,444
Who would turn away from the legacy, and the religion of Ibrahim, except somebody fooling himself.

84
00:04:39,664 --> 00:04:41,624
وَلَقَدِ ٱصْطَفَيْنَـٰهُ فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا

85
00:04:41,774 --> 00:04:44,794
and We had chosen him in worldly life, in this world,

86
00:04:44,794 --> 00:04:46,974
وَإِنَّهُۥ فِى ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ لَمِنَ ٱلصَّـٰلِحِينَ

87
00:04:47,154 --> 00:04:51,064
and certainly, in the afterlife, he is counted, truly among the righteous.

88
00:04:51,174 --> 00:04:53,434
إِذْ قَالَ لَهُۥ رَبُّهُۥٓ أَسْلِمْ

89
00:04:53,654 --> 00:04:56,154
Whenever his Master said to him, 'Submit!'

90
00:04:56,324 --> 00:04:58,169
قَالَ أَسْلَمْتُ لِرَبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

91
00:04:58,309 --> 00:05:02,429
He responded by saying, 'I submit myself before the Master of all peoples'.

92
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:05,930
وَوَصَّىٰ بِهَآ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمُ بَنِيهِ وَيَعْقُوبُ

93
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:11,590
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) counselled his children, as did Jacob (يعقوب) his grandson,

94
00:05:11,858 --> 00:05:17,238
So Ibrahim and Ya'qub, grandfather and grandson, both counselled their children the same way.

95
00:05:17,218 --> 00:05:19,568
يَـٰبَنِىَّ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱصْطَفَىٰ لَكُمُ ٱلدِّينَ

96
00:05:19,738 --> 00:05:24,638
My children, it is no doubt Allah, Himself, has chosen the religion for you.

97
00:05:24,668 --> 00:05:26,708
فَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنتُم مُّسْلِمُونَ

98
00:05:26,748 --> 00:05:30,961
then don't you dare find death, except that you are in a state of being Muslim

99
00:05:31,181 --> 00:05:33,681
أَمْ كُنتُمْ شُهَدَآءَ إِذْ حَضَرَ يَعْقُوبَ ٱلْمَوْتُ

100
00:05:33,751 --> 00:05:38,161
Were you witness when death presented itself to Jacob, to Ya'qub?

101
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,641
إِذْ قَالَ لِبَنِيهِ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِنۢ بَعْدِى

102
00:05:40,801 --> 00:05:45,181
When he said to his sons, 'What are you going to worship?', at that moment he said to his sons,

103
00:05:45,181 --> 00:05:47,968
'What will you worship after me, much after me?'

104
00:05:48,228 --> 00:05:49,588
قَالُوا۟ نَعْبُدُ إِلَـٰهَكَ

105
00:05:49,738 --> 00:05:51,368
They said: 'We will worship your God'

106
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:54,788
وَإِلَـٰهَ ءَابَآئِكَ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ وَإِسْمَـٰعِيلَ وَإِسْحَـٰقَ

107
00:05:54,798 --> 00:06:00,368
and the God of your fathers, the Ilah, deity of your fathers: Ibrahim, Isma'il, Ishaaq.

108
00:06:00,511 --> 00:06:01,551
إِلَـٰهًۭا وَٰحِدًۭا

109
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:03,471
All of which is one, same God.

110
00:06:03,601 --> 00:06:04,881
وَنَحْنُ لَهُۥ مُسْلِمُونَ

111
00:06:06,181 --> 00:06:10,021
And we are only, and only, submissive or Muslim before Him.

112
00:06:10,141 --> 00:06:15,241
This is a brief, quick translation of 122 to 133, okay? These Āyāt.

113
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:18,260
What I'd like to start off with, this is not

114
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:21,160
unlike the previous section, in which I was telling you

115
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:24,110
the progressive development of arguments, which is also happening here.

116
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,740
But my goal now is to highlight something else entirely.

117
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:30,040
What I'm going to try to do is to show you associations.

118
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:33,650
There are sets of Āyāt that have similar subject matter.

119
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,540
And I'm going to write those out for you first.

120
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,400
I think that's probably the logical way to get to the

121
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,360
point where I teach you what I want to teach you.

122
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,650
So I'm gonna put some numbers here. I'm gonna write

123
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:45,060
something that can't be written.

124
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:47,560
Okay.

125
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:53,450
So, all right, so there are some associations. Let's first spell that out for you.

126
00:06:53,450 --> 00:06:57,060
Before we write the associations. The Israelites are told to be grateful.

127
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:01,679
يَـٰبَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱذْكُرُوا۟ نِعْمَتِىَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَنِّى فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

128
00:07:01,699 --> 00:07:05,279
Don't write anything down yet, just listen. Just see if you understand the association.

129
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:10,299
They are told to be, to mention the favour of Allah on them.

130
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,050
That Allah gave them preference over all other nations.

131
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,849
Where did that favour begin?

132
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,959
With Ibrahim عليه السلام.

133
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,990
And actually, by the end of this passage, Allah says,

134
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,189
Who would turn away from Ibrahim's عليه السلام legacy but a fool?

135
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,160
And when Allah chose them over all nations,

136
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:30,960
He's also telling the Israelites, your father, Ya'qub.

137
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:33,282
By the way, what's the other name of Ya'qub?

138
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,640
Isra'il.

139
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:37,020
Isra'il told his children,

140
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:39,160
'Don't die, except that you're Muslim.'

141
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,310
And they said, Of course we won't.'

142
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:43,860
'We're going to stick to the legacy of your father, Ibrahim.'

143
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:48,520
So there is an association between two sets of Āyāt. I'm gonna put them here.

144
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:51,960
122 and 130 to 132.

145
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:55,350
In 122, the Israelites are being told.

146
00:07:56,040 --> 00:08:01,040
You know, be grateful for the legacy-- for the favour I gave you. In 130 to 132

147
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,890
it's that favour itself. What is that favour?

148
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:06,320
That favour is, you took the same promise from your father.

149
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,750
You received the same gift from your father that

150
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,940
you're-- that his grandfather gave to his son.

151
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:14,806
Ibrahim gave to Ishaaq, Ishaaq gave to Ya'qub, Ya'qub/Isra'il gave to you.

152
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:17,646
Don't you die! Except that you're in Islam.

153
00:08:17,636 --> 00:08:19,920
You see the association, that argument?

154
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:23,260
Okay, so that's the favour on the Israelites.

155
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,860
The favour of Islam

156
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,050
on the Israelites.

157
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,159
Ibrahim عليه السلام was made leader over all people, yes?

158
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:37,429
And he was told--he asked what about my kids?

159
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:41,760
And Allah said my promise doesn't extend to wrongdoers.

160
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:45,650
Then Ibrahim عليه السلام comes, comes up with a counter offer.

161
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:49,330
He says, Well, can You at least make sure I and my son Isma'il,

162
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:50,760
as we're building the Ka'bah,

163
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:52,710
can we be accepted as Muslim?

164
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:56,820
