It has to be a balance of both things.

402
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:38,412
Just like night and day are balanced with each other. On the one end was

403
00:21:38,392 --> 00:21:39,502
وَخَلَقْنَـٰكُمْ أَزْوَٰجًۭا
 and

404
00:21:39,492 --> 00:21:40,932
وَجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًۭا

405
00:21:40,922 --> 00:21:43,806
But the most remarkable thing in this passage is that He said

406
00:21:43,810 --> 00:21:45,730
Your sleep was cut off.

407
00:21:46,856 --> 00:21:49,249
Your sleep was made something that cuts you off.

408
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:51,259
What does sleep cut you off from?

409
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:53,970
Everything.

410
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,960
Your problems, your concerns.

411
00:21:56,340 --> 00:22:00,600
The thing is though everything in this passage from beginning to end is paired.

412
00:22:01,340 --> 00:22:04,460
Earth is paired with mountain, just like sky is paired with the sun.

413
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:07,670
Man is paired with woman just like what?

414
00:22:08,540 --> 00:22:10,270
Night is paired with day.

415
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:16,260
If everything is paired, then sleep should be paired with what?

416
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,460
Waking up.

417
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:20,560
Deliberately,

418
00:22:20,570 --> 00:22:23,230
all things mentioned in the passage are in pairs,

419
00:22:23,230 --> 00:22:26,270
and one thing has been excluded from its pair.

420
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:30,360
But it's pair should be obvious to you. What's the pair to sleeping?

421
00:22:31,340 --> 00:22:34,049
What's the message of Ṣūrah al-Naba?

422
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:38,324
Day of judgment. When humanity will

423
00:22:38,834 --> 00:22:39,605
wake up?

424
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:44,030
When you say that sleep, obviously the pair is waking up.

425
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:48,660
It doesn't even have to be said. It's a conclusion that you can arrive all on your own.

426
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:53,490
Qurʾān centralizes the notion of sleep cutting you off,

427
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:56,270
and it's obvious to you that after sleep comes

428
00:22:56,740 --> 00:22:57,610
waking up.

429
00:22:57,620 --> 00:23:00,830
So why isn't it obvious to you that after your sleep in your grave,

430
00:23:00,830 --> 00:23:01,960
there's also a waking up.

431
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:06,870
That should be a conclusion. You should be able to arrive on your own.

432
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:09,840
It's like Allah deliberately left it out.

433
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,160
So you have an aha moment because you're gonna be waking up.

434
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:16,940
And just like waking up is supposed to happen at a specific time,

435
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:18,860
because even if you're a believer or non believer,

436
00:23:18,870 --> 00:23:21,405
you have to get up by a certain time to get certain tasks done.

437
00:23:21,785 --> 00:23:23,890
إِنَّ يَوْمَ ٱلْفَصْلِ كَانَ

438
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:25,254
مِيقَـٰتًۭا

439
00:23:25,284 --> 00:23:26,410
At a particular time.

440
00:23:26,990 --> 00:23:28,010
From (وقت)

441
00:23:28,020 --> 00:23:29,112
كَانَ مِيقَـٰتًۭا

442
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:33,170
It's actually supposed to go at-- the alarm is supposed to go off at a certain time.

443
00:23:33,740 --> 00:23:37,370
And remarkably, (ٱلْفَصْلِ) also means separation.

444
00:23:37,570 --> 00:23:39,170
Just like (سبات) does.

445
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:43,360
Sleep cuts you off, and that waking will cut you off from your sleep.

446
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:45,690
First, you're cut off from waking up.

447
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:46,900
Then you're gonna get cut off from your sleep and you will fall asleep. And

448
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,491
إِنَّ يَوْمَ ٱلْفَصْلِ كَانَ مِيقَـٰتًۭا

449
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:49,396
SubhanAllah.

450
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:51,770
Okay? So,

451
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:55,640
this would be my second brief example of, you know,

452
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:59,100
passages and how the themes bind into one another.

453
00:23:59,110 --> 00:24:02,820
Some of the most interesting are actually we're going to see in in Ṣūrah al-Yāsīn.

454
00:24:02,830 --> 00:24:04,650
And I'm going to colour code those for you.

455
00:24:04,650 --> 00:24:07,273
So you can see what's happening in the first passage of Ṣūrah al-Yāsīn.

456
00:24:07,290 --> 00:24:09,263
Even though, in my estimation

457
00:24:09,940 --> 00:24:12,850
Ṣūrah al-Yāsīn is broken up into 6 passages.

458
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:15,360
We might do all of Ṣūrah al-Yāsīn tomorrow, Inshallah.

459
00:24:15,740 --> 00:24:19,670
It's broken up into 6 passages and each one of them is a perfect ring.

460
00:24:21,140 --> 00:24:23,860
And all together, all 6 form a perfect ring.

461
00:24:24,740 --> 00:24:25,760
So it's actually

462
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:27,705
كُلٌّۭ فِى فَلَكٍۢ يَسْبَحُونَ

463
00:24:27,715 --> 00:24:28,903
It's remarkable

464
00:24:29,340 --> 00:24:32,180
how Ṣūrah al-Yāsīn is organized so well, I'll stop at this.

465
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:33,483
Inshallah ta'ala, we'll pray maghrib.

